Step-by-Step Guide: CI/CD for Dynamics 365 using GitHub Actions (Pattern A)
1. Overview
Pattern A uses the DEV environment as the source of truth. The CI pipeline exports unmanaged solutions from DEV, unpacks them into Git, and runs Solution Checker. The Build pipeline exports managed solutions from DEV and stores them as artifacts. The CD pipeline imports managed solutions into TEST and PROD environments using deployment settings files for connection references and environment variables.
2. Prerequisites
1.	1. Create three Dataverse environments: DEV, TEST, PROD (each with a database). (Done)
2.	2. Create an Azure AD App Registration (service principal) and generate a client secret. (Done)
3.	3. Grant Dynamics CRM API permissions and create an Application User in each environment with System Administrator role. (Done)
4.	4. Prepare GitHub repository and add secrets: PP_APP_ID, PP_TENANT_ID, PP_CLIENT_SECRET, DEV_ENV_URL, TEST_ENV_URL, PROD_ENV_URL.
3. Tool Installation
5.	1. Power Platform CLI (PAC) for local testing: pac install latest
6.	2. Node.js (for PCF controls, optional for Pattern A)
7.	3. .NET SDK (for plug-in assemblies, optional for Pattern A)
4. GitHub Setup
Create a GitHub repository and configure Actions secrets:
- PP_APP_ID
- PP_TENANT_ID
- PP_CLIENT_SECRET
- DEV_ENV_URL
- TEST_ENV_URL
- PROD_ENV_URL
5. Deployment Settings
Create JSON files for TEST and PROD environments under pipelines/settings/ directory. These files map environment variables and connection references.
Example deploy.test.json:
{
  "EnvironmentVariables": [
    { "SchemaName": "new_BackendApiBaseUrl", "Value": "https://test.api.contoso.local" },
    { "SchemaName": "new_NotificationToEmail", "Value": "crm-test@contoso.com" }
  ],
  "ConnectionReferences": [
    {
      "LogicalName": "new_sharedsharepointonline",
      "ConnectionId": "c1b6d99e-0f9a-4b9f-9be1-1b715a1e8a11",
      "ConnectorId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_sharepointonline"
    }
  ]
}
6. CI Workflow
Purpose: Export unmanaged solution from DEV, unpack, run Solution Checker, and commit changes.
name: CI – Export & Unpack from DEV
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]
jobs:
  export_unpack_check:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Install Power Platform Tools
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/actions-install@v1
      - name: WhoAmI
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/who-am-i@v1
        with:
          environment-url: ${{ secrets.DEV_ENV_URL }}
          app-id: ${{ secrets.PP_APP_ID }}
          client-secret: ${{ secrets.PP_CLIENT_SECRET }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.PP_TENANT_ID }}
      - name: Export unmanaged solution
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/export-solution@v1
        with:
          environment-url: ${{ secrets.DEV_ENV_URL }}
          app-id: ${{ secrets.PP_APP_ID }}
          client-secret: ${{ secrets.PP_CLIENT_SECRET }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.PP_TENANT_ID }}
          solution-name: YourSolutionName
          managed: false
          solution-output-file: out/YourSolutionName_unmanaged.zip
      - name: Unpack solution
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/unpack-solution@v1
        with:
          solution-file: out/YourSolutionName_unmanaged.zip
          solution-folder: solutions/YourSolutionName
          overwrite-files: true
      - name: Run Solution Checker
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/check-solution@v1
        with:
          environment-url: ${{ secrets.DEV_ENV_URL }}
          app-id: ${{ secrets.PP_APP_ID }}
          client-secret: ${{ secrets.PP_CLIENT_SECRET }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.PP_TENANT_ID }}
          solution-file: out/YourSolutionName_unmanaged.zip
      - name: Commit changes
        run: |
          git config user.name "github-actions"
          git config user.email "actions@github.com"
          git add solutions/YourSolutionName
          git commit -m "Unpacked solution from DEV" || echo "No changes"
          git push

7. Build Workflow
Purpose: Export managed solution from DEV and upload as artifact.
name: Build – Managed Solution
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]
    paths:
      - 'solutions/YourSolutionName/**'
jobs:
  build_managed:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Install Power Platform Tools
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/actions-install@v1
      - name: Export managed solution
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/export-solution@v1
        with:
          environment-url: ${{ secrets.DEV_ENV_URL }}
          app-id: ${{ secrets.PP_APP_ID }}
          client-secret: ${{ secrets.PP_CLIENT_SECRET }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.PP_TENANT_ID }}
          solution-name: YourSolutionName
          managed: true
          solution-output-file: drop/YourSolutionName_managed.zip
      - name: Upload artifact
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: managed-solution
          path: drop/YourSolutionName_managed.zip

8. CD Workflow
Purpose: Import managed solution into TEST or PROD using deployment settings file.
name: Deploy – TEST & PROD
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      environment:
        description: 'Target environment'
        required: true
        type: choice
        options: [ TEST, PROD ]
      artifactName:
        description: 'Artifact name'
        required: true
        default: 'managed-solution'
jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    environment: ${{ github.event.inputs.environment == 'PROD' && 'prod' || 'test' }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: ${{ github.event.inputs.artifactName }}
      - name: Install Power Platform Tools
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/actions-install@v1
      - name: Import managed solution
        uses: microsoft/powerplatform-actions/import-solution@v1
        with:
          environment-url: ${{ github.event.inputs.environment == 'PROD' && secrets.PROD_ENV_URL || secrets.TEST_ENV_URL }}
          app-id: ${{ secrets.PP_APP_ID }}
          client-secret: ${{ secrets.PP_CLIENT_SECRET }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.PP_TENANT_ID }}
          solution-file: YourSolutionName_managed.zip
          publish-changes: true
          activate-plugins: true
          use-deployment-settings-file: true
          deployment-settings-file: ${{ github.event.inputs.environment == 'PROD' && 'pipelines/settings/deploy.prod.json' || 'pipelines/settings/deploy.test.json' }}

9. Verification
8.	1. Check GitHub Actions logs for successful execution of each step.
9.	2. Verify solution imported in TEST and PROD environments.
10.	3. Ensure flows are active and plug-in steps are enabled.
11.	4. Validate PCF controls render correctly in apps.
10. Troubleshooting
12.	1. Ensure actions-install@v1 is the first step in each workflow.
13.	2. Verify GitHub secrets and Application User permissions.
14.	3. Check deployment settings file for correct connection references and environment variables.
15.	4. Set force-overwrite to true only if you intend to overwrite unmanaged customizations.
